==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|de}} {{term|Centromer}}, corresponding to {{term|centro-}} + {{etyl|grc}} {{term|μέρος||part|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈsɛntɹə(ʊ)mɪə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|genetics}} The central region of a [[eukaryotic]] [[chromosome]] where the [[kinetochore]] is assembled.
#* '''1999''', {{w|Matt Ridley}}, ''Genome'', Harper Perennial 2000, p. 16:
#*: Every chromosome has a long arm and a short arm separated by a pinch point known as a '''centromere'''.

